@page "/HowItWorks/limitations"
@using InvestmentTaxCalculator.Components

<HowItWorksGuideLayout PageAddress="HowItWorks/limitations">
    <ChildContent>
        <div class="section">
            <p>
                The app handles the common cases for a private investor. These rules and situations are not covered, so check
                them yourself if they apply to you.
            </p>
            <h2 class="section-title">Capital gains</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Taper relief, and other reliefs and elections, are not applied.</li>
                <li>
                    Gains on non-reporting offshore funds are taxed as income (offshore income gains). The app treats them as
                    ordinary capital gains.
                </li>
                <li>
                    The rule for a reporting fund sold before the end of a reporting period and bought back within 30 days
                    after it is not applied (see <a href="HowItWorks/reporting-funds" class="link-styled">Excess reportable
                    income and equalisation</a>).
                </li>
                <li>
                    Trade dates are used as they appear in your broker statement, without converting time zones. A trade near
                    midnight can fall on a different UK date.
                </li>
                <li>Purchases inside an ISA or pension are not seen unless you import them, so they are never matched.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="section-title">Options and futures</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Futures settled by delivery are not supported.</li>
                <li>The app does not check whether a futures contract is traded on a recognised futures exchange.</li>
                <li>
                    Tax refunds for written options closed in a later tax year are listed for you to claim. They are not
                    entered on any form for you.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="section-title">Income and residency</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>The app does not decide your residency status, and has no separate setting for "Treaty non-resident" periods.</li>
                <li>Margin interest and other investment expenses are not deducted.</li>
                <li>
                    Excess reportable income, equalisation, takeovers and spin-offs are not reported by brokers, so they are only
                    included if you add them.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </ChildContent>
    <FurtherReading>
        <li><a href="HowItWorks" class="link-styled">All guides</a></li>
    </FurtherReading>
</HowItWorksGuideLayout>
